			<div class="content" id="post-content-1525078">
									

<p>Point 1: It's the sudden impulse to chop off/cut out a (likely not-insignificant) portion of your body, from people with absolutely no prior or subsequent signs of OCD or any other related mental illness. It always pops up in four simultaneous people at the same time, who were doing the same thing (which I'll address below) and cut off the same part (I think.) That's beyond coincidence, and mental disorders of that caliber do not typically just pop into existence for a single, isolated incident, and then vanish completely forever.</p>
<p>They're able to determine that everyone was doing the same thing at the same time, because four different people in four different parts of the country/world all were asked &quot;So what exactly prompted you to chop off your left thumb?&quot; and their answers were were *all* some permutation of &quot;Well, I was just sitting there eating a BLT, when I got this sensation that my thumb wasn't really MY thumb, and it had to go.&quot; Again, that's well beyond coincidence territory, especially when it happens again and again. Well I guess they can't exactly ask that if the people bleed to death, or if they feel like their larynx or lower mandible is the part that needs to be excised, but you get the point.</p>

